          (unit 1)))))
  (text
    "12V INPUT PROTECTION (LM74800-Q1, common-drain back-to-back NFETs, per TI LM7480-Q1 DS SNOSD95C Fig.10-1)\n- Q101 (DGATE) = ideal diode / reverse-battery; Q102 (HGATE) = overvoltage cut-off.\n- OV cut-off = 1.231V x (470k+39k)/39k = ~16.1V (protects TPS568230 18V / TPS62130 17V abs-max downstream).\n- UVLO rising = 1.231V x (220k+40.2k)/40.2k = ~8.0V.\n- LM7480 exposed pad (RTN) must be left FLOATING - do not tie to GND copper (DS Table 6-1).\n- Fuse/TVS/FET MPNs are proposals - VERIFY ratings and inrush (3x(2x220uF)+bulk) before ordering.\nSYSTEM RAILS\n- +3V3: LM61460-Q1 (substitute for backordered LMQ61460-Q1; same RJR-14 pinout per both TI datasheets), Vout=1V x (1+100k/43.2k)=3.31V, 400kHz.\n- +0V95 (PI7C9X3G606GP VDDC/VP/C_VDDC, worst ~3.3A @Tj80C per DS Table 12-12): TPS568230, Vref 0.6V, 5.62k/9.53k -> 0.954V, FCCM 800kHz.\n- +1V8 (PI7C VDDR/VPH/C_VDDR ~0.25A + EEPROM + PCA9306): TPS62130, 150k/120k -> 1.80V.\n- +1V2 (USB5744 VDD12, 688mA typ with 4 SS ports per DS Table 10-3): TPS62130, 75k/150k -> 1.20V.\n- Low-voltage regulators enabled by PG_3V3 (simple sequencing; PI7C requires PERST# held until rails+REFCLK stable)."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20.32 285 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "d19a484a-0f34-5d7a-a2cc-c4a409f5cc22"))
